Subject: [PATCH] transmission: avoid Darwin Ninja RPATH relink in bundled NAT libs

The bundled MiniUPnPc and libnatpmp external projects build small helper
executables in addition to static libraries. On Darwin targets, CMake cannot
perform the install-time RPATH relink step with the Ninja generator. Build them
with the install RPATH from the start; the packaged Transmission output only
uses the static libraries.

diff -ruN -U0 a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-07-06 00:00:00
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-07-06 00:00:00
@@ -520 +520,2 @@
-        -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF)
+        -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF
+        -DCMAKE_BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH=ON)
@@ -538,2 +539,3 @@
-        -DUPNPC_BUILD_SHARED=OFF
-        -DUPNPC_BUILD_TESTS=OFF)
+        -DUPNPC_BUILD_SHARED=OFF
+        -DUPNPC_BUILD_TESTS=OFF
+        -DCMAKE_BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH=ON)
